  not a self s this is not a vendor event  so it sounds like the future is moving  beyond kubernetes and figuring out what  we can do with the building blocks that  kubernetes is offered  yeah I think that's actually it I'm  kubernetes was never supposed to be  end-all be-all it's basically you know  it's computing networking storage  everything else needs to be provided  outside and I'm I'll speak for VMware in  a little bit because you know we've been  doing this literally for twenty years  now  you know this basically the  software-defined data center what we're  seeing is now that I'm growing in this  cloud native ways it just opens up so  much space and then you know looking at  what Google did you know Google starts  in the ad space and then you know got  really good at compute but now you're  seeing that we all need to move in a  different direction because  unfortunately you know none of us have  cracked this not yet and that's great  that's amazing that means we're making  progress and we haven't stagnated yet so  one of the really cool things I've seen  at the conference was the mental health  session I think it was born out of the  realization that folks are starting to  burn out in the community can you talk a  little bit about that when we did  Seattle back in December we have we  always have a retrospective session it's  like really the last session the last  day anyone who wants to come there's a  lot of sentiment cinnamon in that room  where you know this is hard and you know  you want to go to all the talks and you  want us to meet all the people and you  know we're humans and we can't handle  that so we always were paying attention  to it but Sheryl hung who works with CN  CF she actually wanted the extra stuff  and they coordinated with people that  they could actually have in booth  downstairs in the sponsor showcase that  you could talk to if you get burnt out  but I also want to encourage anyone if  you think about this a conference is  just th